{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments","id":892970,"title":"Let's Cook Up Some Crown Attainments","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-17T20:07:02-07:00","id":892970,"title":"Let's Cook Up Some Crown Attainments","content":"So we have Crown Attainments for Forces, Mind, Prime, and Space. Let's make some for the rest of the Arcana.<br /> <br /> Looking at the existing Crowns, the following things stand out:<br /> <br /> \u2022 They are obviously themed after the Exarch in question. So Life's Crown Attainment is going to be the Crown of Predation, not the Crown of Growth.<br /> \u2022 They consist of two benefits.<br /> \u2022 The first benefit is roughly equivalent to a Utility Attainment, but a bit better - remove the Mana cost for something, get a new way to recover Mana, etcetera.<br /> \u2022 The second benefit scales with the Arcana rating, and look like they're more focused on countering penalties than supplying bonuses.<br /> <br /> Given that we have four examples, the last two bulletpoints are negotiable.<br /> <br /> (I'll try to come up with one after I get done with my studying, if I don't immediately go to bed.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T20:16:16-07:00","id":892980,"title":"","content":"The main reason additional prelacies don't exist is because it seems that only the Exarchs in ascendancy within the Seers are capable of manifesting the power to develop them. Other than that, cheers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T20:19:46-07:00","id":892982,"title":"","content":"For reference, the other Exarchs:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seers of the Throne</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Chancellor: The Exarch of Matter promotes corporate capitalism and the commoditization of every resource. Water, air, people \u2014 they should all have a price, owner, and the ability to be bought and sold for profit. The Chancellor\u2019s star rises under his Ministry of Mammon, and Seers whisper that he\u2019ll one day be recognized as an Archigenitor. <br /> <br /> The Nemesis: This Exarch enforces the division between flesh and spirit. The Shadow represents an untamed part of the Fallen World that even the Ex-archs cannot bring to heel. The Spirit Seal lets human ignorance and passions breed monsters in the Shadow, but it conceals the arts that shamans and traditional sorcerers use to placate and bind them.<br /> <br /> The Psychopomp: Death\u2019s Seal commands souls. Barring them from Stygia\u2019s release, it condemns them to abide in numerous incarnations or erode into gray shades. If there is a heaven, the Psychopomp guards the way with a sword, and will only let the greatest Seers enter.<br /> <br /> The Prophet: This Exarch\u2019s followers say Time is propelled by the actions of the elect upon the guileless masses. The ideal Seer is a \u201cGreat Man\u201d who drives history toward an inevitable triumph; Sleepers must follow in lockstep or be crushed beneath the tide.<br /> <br /> The Raptor: The Seal of Life promotes faith in natural law, unleavened by free will. The world is predator and prey, rot and renewal, and individuals are helpless to choose how they flow along the world\u2019s life cycle. Instinct and resignation replaces free will.<br /> <br /> The Ruin: Fate\u2019s Seal is the entropy that destroys dreams, relationships and even civilizations. Mystic destinies create new opportunities, but the Ruin en-sures that people are skeptical and cynical about the opportunities ahead of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus our old friend The Gate, who probably doesn't bestow Prelacies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T20:31:46-07:00","id":892988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=892980#post892980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main reason additional prelacies don't exist is because it seems that only the Exarchs in ascendancy within the Seers are capable of manifesting the power to develop them. Other than that, cheers.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't mean that the others aren't going to climb to the top of the heap any time soon, or that they've <i>always</i> been on top.<br /> <br /> If I want to play a historical game, and The Ruin is currently on top (because Rome is falling and decaying)? I'm going to want a mad whack Ruin ninja to show up.<br /> <br /> (I also want Servitors for all of the Arcana. And a pony.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T20:37:34-07:00","id":892994,"title":"","content":"*pays attention for Ruin and Prophet Crowns*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T20:44:00-07:00","id":892996,"title":"","content":"That reminds me: does Pantechnicon have an Exarch as a sponsor? I thought I remembered that it's in competition with Mammon for the Chancellor's favor, but I haven't been able to find anything.<br /> <br /> Edit: Dave mentions it here <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/new-order/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/new-order/</a> in the comments, so never mind. I guess I should think of something for the Chancellor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":61,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","user":"Octavo","date":". 05-17-2016, 11:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T20:52:05-07:00","id":893001,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking that The Nemesis' Crown should either raise or lower the nearby effective Gauntlet rating by one, but can't decide between the two. Raising it falls in with the idea that the Exarchs shun the Shadow for not being their domain, but that screws over the Prelate who is hopefully decent at Spirit magic; lowering the Gauntlet is beneficial to the Prelate and allows spirits to run amok and terrify Sleepers, but is out of tune with the existing fluff.<br /> <br /> It's a shame Honorary Rank is already the existing Four-Dot Attainment for Spirit, because that would be perfect. Maybe something making it so that Spirit Sight is automatic and separate from Active Mage Sight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T20:52:50-07:00","id":893002,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Pantechnicon and Mammon are competing for the Chancellor's favor. It's one of the main barriers between either and claiming Greater Ministry status.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T21:00:11-07:00","id":893006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=893002#post893002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Pantechnicon and Mammon are competing for the Chancellor's favor. It's one of the main barriers between either and claiming Greater Ministry status.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd pay so much money for a pre-written campaign about uniting them in order to finally topple the Hegemonic Ministry and elevate the Chancellor to Archgenitor status. It would be a blast to actually toss out some stuff aimed at playing as the Seers, and would nicely illustrate the pettiness of the Iron Pyramid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T21:26:51-07:00","id":893014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=893001#post893001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking that The Nemesis' Crown should either raise or lower the nearby effective Gauntlet rating by one, but can't decide between the two. Raising it falls in with the idea that the Exarchs shun the Shadow for not being their domain, but that screws over the Prelate who is hopefully decent at Spirit magic; lowering the Gauntlet is beneficial to the Prelate and allows spirits to run amok and terrify Sleepers, but is out of tune with the existing fluff.<br /> <br /> It's a shame Honorary Rank is already the existing Four-Dot Attainment for Spirit, because that would be perfect. Maybe something making it so that Spirit Sight is automatic and separate from Active Mage Sight?</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'm taking a break:<br /> <br /> It totally should raise the Gauntlet rating by 1 around them (as a passive, always on thing), and let them ignore penalties due to Gauntlet rating equal to their Spirit Dots. Because why not do both?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T22:07:07-07:00","id":893029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=893014#post893014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I'm taking a break:<br /> <br /> It totally should raise the Gauntlet rating by 1 around them (as a passive, always on thing), and let them ignore penalties due to Gauntlet rating equal to their Spirit Dots. Because why not do both?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's elegant and nicely does the job for me. Yay!<br /> <br /> It sounds like a Crown from The Raptor runs afoul of the whole &quot;why are the Thyrsus bad at driving emotions&quot; thing that's been such a hot topic recently. I might want to go for &quot;opponents lose Doors equal to your dots in Life,&quot; except The Unity already covers that. How would you balance a scaling Composure penalty?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T22:27:03-07:00","id":893036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=893029#post893029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that's elegant and nicely does the job for me. Yay!<br /> <br /> It sounds like a Crown from The Raptor runs afoul of the whole &quot;why are the Thyrsus bad at driving emotions&quot; thing that's been such a hot topic recently. I might want to go for &quot;opponents lose Doors equal to your dots in Life,&quot; except The Unity already covers that. How would you balance a scaling Composure penalty?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure; I'm weighing heavily towards &quot;pick something else&quot;, though.<br /> <br /> The scaling benefits (other than Fury's) are all buffs to you that work in a pretty raw way.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The Crown of Unity makes you <i>so</i> good at reading people that you could sell sand in the desert.<br /> \u2022 The Crown of Purity makes your fallen form a better vessal for mana, letting you hold more.<br /> \u2022 The Crown of Vision makes your vision all-piercing.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Crown of Fury... gives you instinctive knowledge on how to counter specific fighting moves.<br /> <br /> I wish Fury had been something more along the lines of &quot;your attacks get Piercing equal to your dots in Forces&quot; or something similarly overwhelming, violent, and direct.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> For the Raptor, I'd honestly lean towards something that rewards you for being <i>primal</i> and <i>instinctual</i>, rather than a way to penalize others.<br /> <br /> I'd say &quot;add Life to your Gnosis for the purposes of your Nimbus&quot;, but that's not very Life, now is it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T22:45:01-07:00","id":893048,"title":"","content":"Here's an odd idea; what if the Crown bestowed by The Raptor negated penalties made on rolls to Force Doors? It encourages devotees to take what they want from others /right now/, nevermind social niceties and the potential consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T00:20:35-07:00","id":893095,"title":"","content":"I can't help but wonder what a Gate prelacy would be like and just what kind of person it would take to earn it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T01:01:56-07:00","id":893111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=893095#post893095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but wonder what a Gate prelacy would be like and just what kind of person it would take to earn it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well there is a secret cult of the Gate. It even has its own Left-Handed Legacy (as in one that's Left-Handed from the perspective of other Seers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T01:07:14-07:00","id":893119,"title":"","content":"It could be a greater amount of paradox control, adding something to your gnosis for the purposes of controlling paradox and the ability to increase paradox die on spells (both your own and others) by spending mana, like how regular mages can spend mana to reduce the paradox on their own spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T09:19:45-07:00","id":893375,"title":"","content":"Maybe the Psychopomp's would have something to do with denying death? Like adding Health boxes or making it harder for damage to roll over into Lethal or Agg? Or would it make it easier for ghosts to form somehow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T09:20:39-07:00","id":893376,"title":"","content":"Ministry of Ruin (Crown of Folly)<br /> <br /> <s>Each chapter, you have a pool of Ruin points equal to your Fate rating. By spending a point of Ruin you can make any mundane action made in your presence be rolled using only a chance die, or cause a successful action to reroll, after you see the result. You may spend a Willpower point to affect a spellcasting roll. Also, characters possessing a Destiny merit may not use it against you. Additionally, you count as a Doom for all such characters.</s>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 05-19-2016, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T10:24:53-07:00","id":893420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=893029#post893029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like a Crown from The Raptor runs afoul of the whole &quot;why are the Thyrsus bad at driving emotions&quot; thing that's been such a hot topic recently.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't get why people say that. The Thyrsus can totally inspire visceral sensations and emotions; in fact, they're better at it in some ways than Mastigos, because they make you feel from your flesh, blood and bones, not your mind. To whom it may concern, remember: thoughts are an adaptation. Life is a continuation of itself, an immortal whole, and individuality is superfluous to its truths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 05-18-2016, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T12:25:04-07:00","id":893515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=893376#post893376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ministry of Ruin (Crown of Folly)<br /> <br /> Each chapter, you have a pool of Ruin points equal to your Fate rating. By spending a point of Ruin you can make any mundane action made in your presence be rolled using only a chance die, or cause a successful action to reroll, after you see the result. You may spend a Willpower point to affect a spellcasting roll. Also, characters possessing a Destiny merit may not use it against you. Additionally, you count as a Doom for all such characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woah.<br /> <br /> I would like to lodge my disagreement with this one. It's <i>way</i> better than the other Crowns.<br /> <br /> Is that Willpower thing &quot;I can spend Willpower to improve my spellcasting rolls&quot; or &quot;I can spend Willpower to use Ruin on a spellcasting roll&quot;?<br /> <br /> I like the &quot;you are the Doom of anyone with Destiny&quot; bit, but I think the scaling bit is... a bit excessive.<br /> <hr /><br /> Here's a few:<br /> <br /> <b>Crown of Fury (Revised)</b><br /> Any physical attack you make ignores Armor or successes from a Dodge equal to your dots in Forces. In addition, you may raise or change your Mage Armor without spending Mana.<br /> <br /> <b>Ministry of the Nemesis (Crown of Boundaries)</b><br /> The Crown of Boundaries increases the local Gauntlet rating by 1; additionally, your Spirit spells ignore penalties from the Gauntlet or other similar sources equal to your dots in Spirit.<br /> <br /> <b>Ministry of the Raptor (Crown of Predation)</b><br /> You may ignore surrender and do not suffer the Beaten Down tilt; conversely, the Beaten Down and Surrender rules are still in force for your opponents even if you are trying to kill them. Additionally, {scaling benefit}.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T13:40:12-07:00","id":893565,"title":"","content":"Being a Doom of everyone with Destiny is the only part I'm proud of. Unfortunately, while it would have been pretty good in the 1st Edition, now it barely does anything mechanically. Still, I kept it for the flavor.<br /> <br /> The rest of the Crown was supposed to work like an inverted Destiny merit. Hence, a Willpower expenditure is for Ruining a spellcasting roll. I assumed a Rote quality and Chance Die are opposites and that limiting the number of uses balances the effect. Now I think I've gone ahead of myself.<br /> <br /> If I make the Crown suppress the Destiny merit, like Crown of Vision does with Occultation, I will still need an additional bonus. The Doom effect is flavorful, but kind of weak. Do you have any suggestions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T14:48:45-07:00","id":893632,"title":"","content":"Opposite of Rote Quality is &quot;roll twice, pick worse result&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T15:53:26-07:00","id":893687,"title":"","content":"A (kind of funny) idea is that the Crown of Ruin lets people get Willpower for downgrading Failures to Exceptional Failures. So things around you fail <i>explosively</i> much more often. Replace that Willpower with Mana for you personally, and it seems rather lovely. Another idea is to clamp down on Willpower spending <i>entirely</i> - spending Willpower causes you to suffer a Dramatic Failure on a Failure <i>instead</i> of giving you bonus dice, so why even try?<br /> <br /> It might be imposing my own opinions a bit, but I think that Attainments should be as &quot;passive&quot; as possible - they should augment pre-existing options (Crown of Fury making Mage Armor free) or add to your suite of options (sympathetic casting).<br /> <br /> I mean, you are <i>effortlessly and continuously</i> channelling the nature of an Exarch, so I think it should be an &quot;always on&quot; thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T01:20:14-07:00","id":893895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=893632#post893632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Opposite of Rote Quality is &quot;roll twice, pick worse result&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Applied before rolling or after seeing the result?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=893687#post893687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A (kind of funny) idea is that the Crown of Ruin lets people get Willpower for downgrading Failures to Exceptional Failures. So things around you fail <i>explosively</i> much more often. Replace that Willpower with Mana for you personally, and it seems rather lovely. Another idea is to clamp down on Willpower spending <i>entirely</i> - spending Willpower causes you to suffer a Dramatic Failure on a Failure <i>instead</i> of giving you bonus dice, so why even try?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's great thematically and works for an NPC Seer, but less so for a PC. It assumes the NPCs spend Willpower and that's not something every GM is willing to track. Then again, the same can be said about the Destiny merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=893687#post893687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be imposing my own opinions a bit, but I think that Attainments should be as &quot;passive&quot; as possible - they should augment pre-existing options (Crown of Fury making Mage Armor free) or add to your suite of options (sympathetic casting).<br /> <br /> I mean, you are <i>effortlessly and continuously</i> channelling the nature of an Exarch, so I think it should be an &quot;always on&quot; thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm convinced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T09:02:58-07:00","id":894064,"title":"","content":"\u201cThey say all the Iron Seals have Prelacies, but only<br /> the Archigenitors routinely grant them. Regardless of<br /> Ministry, any Seer with the prerequisite Status and<br /> Dream Merits can learn them. When a Ministry sees<br /> the rise of a particular Prelacy in its ranks, it\u2019s a sign<br /> of flowering greatness. When a Ministry\u2019s signature<br /> Prelacy falls out of favor, it\u2019s an ill omen; the Ministry<br /> will fall. The Hegemonic Ministry hasn\u2019t reached this<br /> point, but both members and outsiders watch for it.\u201d<br /> <br /> --- Seers of the Throne 1e book.<br /> I think that the non-Archigenitor prelacies should either be slightly weaker than their Archigenitor counterparts, or, the prelates of the lesser ministries are a lot more rare, and this could be compounded by making the prelacy merit either cost more, or \u201ccost more\u201d in the story itself, a more harrowing or difficult astral quest to gain the Exarch\u2019s favor, for example. That or the prelacy can only go as far as crown and can\u2019t go as high as Temple?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=893095#post893095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but wonder what a Gate prelacy would be like and just what kind of person it would take to earn it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Gatekeepers segregate themselves according to either being Openers or Closers. If the Gate did have a prelacy it would reflect this, one half of the attainment would be useful for \u201copening\u201d the abyss, and the other \u201cclosing it\u201d, that, or you\u2019d have a separate prelacy for openers and closers.<br /> Each Ministry is meant to regulate something within the Exarch\u2019s themes, and what Gatekeepers regulate is the abyss itself, helping or hindering it to \u201ctrim\u201d the fallen world.<br /> Also, openers and closers don\u2019t get along :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=893565#post893565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being a Doom of everyone with Destiny is the only part I'm proud of. Unfortunately, while it would have been pretty good in the 1st Edition, now it barely does anything mechanically. Still, I kept it for the flavor.<br /> <br /> The rest of the Crown was supposed to work like an inverted Destiny merit. Hence, a Willpower expenditure is for Ruining a spellcasting roll. I assumed a Rote quality and Chance Die are opposites and that limiting the number of uses balances the effect. Now I think I've gone ahead of myself.<br /> <br /> If I make the Crown suppress the Destiny merit, like Crown of Vision does with Occultation, I will still need an additional bonus. The Doom effect is flavorful, but kind of weak. Do you have any suggestions?</div> </div> </div> </div>What is Serendipity was always active and its Reach effects vary depending on the strength of the Ruin\u2019s Ministry at any one time? But perhaps not. The theme of the prelacies seems to be a greater trust of the Exarch for the Prelate to regulate the fallen world according to the Arcanum and the Exarch\u2019s wishes. Regulation here is the keyword. So Regulating Fate, the Prelate obviously reduces the Destiny or rote/8-again actions of those opposing the Prelate, but what benefit could the Ruin give that helps the Prelate, but is still toward the goal of regulation?<br /> <br /> But I guess something like Serendipity is a good start.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh oh oh, hideous idea. Awful. Terrible. Unacceptable. Prelates of the Ruin (especially if its archigenitor) get exceptional successes on mundane actions at 3 successes instead of 5--at all times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T09:13:27-07:00","id":894074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=894064#post894064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Oh oh oh, hideous idea. Awful. Terrible. Unacceptable. Prelates of the Ruin (especially if its archigenitor) get exceptional successes on mundane actions at 3 successes instead of 5--at all times.</div> </div> </div> </div>When acting in accordance with the Mystery Visions sent by the Ruin, or when advancing its cause, might be saner.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T09:18:42-07:00","id":894079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=894074#post894074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When acting in accordance with the Mystery Visions sent by the Ruin, or when advancing its cause, might be saner.</div> </div> </div> </div>I almost think that goes without saying, but a good clarification all the same! Course, if a Prelate wasn't in accordance with their Exarch at all times anyway I think they'd be in huge trouble...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T11:58:39-07:00","id":894217,"title":"","content":"FYI, Dave just said on 4chan that the Prelacy of the Chancellor/Matter is that of Scarcity, and the Prophet/Time is of Agency. He also linked to some 1e work of his: forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default9b2e-6.html?g=posts&amp;m=385476#post385476","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 05-19-2016, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T12:41:09-07:00","id":894242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=894217#post894217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">FYI, Dave just said on 4chan that the Prelacy of the Chancellor/Matter is that of Scarcity, and the Prophet/Time is of Agency. He also linked to some 1e work of his: forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default9b2e-6.html?g=posts&amp;m=385476#post385476</div> </div> </div> </div>I took a crack at converting those to 2E.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Poiret One\">Crown of Scarcity</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">In the hands of the Prelate, the use of an item is determined by its cost. The equipment bonus of any mundane item or Imbued item or Artifact of equal to or lesser dot value to the Prelate's Matter Arcanum is disregarded, and the Resource dot value of the item used instead.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">A Prelate of the Chancellor knows there is power in one's possessions. She may dedicate as many magical tools as she has dots in the Matter Arcanum.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Poiret One\">Crown of Agency</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Seers devoted to the Prophet may have to act against the Great and the Good in service of their Exarch. When she faces one who can move Earth, the Prelate falls back on her service to one who moves Heaven. The Seer may ignore the effects of Status Merits or Destiny dice used directly against her up to her Time Arcanum.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Seer may also ignore one point of Withstand when casting a spell using the Temporal Sympathy attainment. </span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T03:36:07-07:00","id":897667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=893515#post893515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Ministry of the Raptor (Crown of Predation)</b><br /> You may ignore surrender and do not suffer the Beaten Down tilt; conversely, the Beaten Down and Surrender rules are still in force for your opponents even if you are trying to kill them. Additionally, {scaling benefit}.</div> </div> </div> </div>What did you think of the suggestion to ignore up to [Life] penalties to Force Doors?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T12:32:57-07:00","id":898088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=897667#post897667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did you think of the suggestion to ignore up to [Life] penalties to Force Doors?</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with that one is that the Crown of Unity already does that as a side effect of reducing the number of doors - so it would just feel redundant and kinda like getting the short end of the stick.<br /> <br /> Part of me was thinking that you could add your Life dots to Down and Dirty rolls, or something to that effect - give them a real alpha-predator type deal.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> It'd also probably also make their go-to method of dealing with people punching them in the face. That is fine too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T06:24:02-07:00","id":904910,"title":"","content":"So right now we have:<br /> <br /> <b>Crown of Obligation</b><br /> The character gains an additional Vice, and regains one point of Mana every time she gains Willpower through either Vice. Also, she reduces opponent\u2019s Doors in Social maneuvering by her Mind dots<br /> <br /> <b>Crown of Vision </b><br /> When using the Sympathetic Range Attainment, the character counts as having a weak sympathetic connection to any subject she has no connection for. She reduces the effects of Occultation and similar powers by her Space dots<br /> _<br /> <br /> <b>Crown of Doctrine</b><br /> The character adds her Prime dots to her Gnosis to determine her Mana pool (every effective dot above 10 grants 10 extra Mana), and may heal resistant damage by Pattern restoration<br /> <br /> <b>Crown of Fury (Revised)</b><br /> Any physical attack, the character makes ignores Armor or successes from a Dodge equal to her dots in Forces. In addition, she may raise or change her Mage Armor without spending Mana.<br /> _<br /> <br /> <b>Ministry of the Nemesis (Crown of Boundaries)</b><br /> The Crown of Boundaries increases the local Gauntlet rating by 1; additionally, the character's Spirit spells ignore penalties from the Gauntlet or other similar sources equal to her dots in Spirit.<br /> <br /> <b>Ministry of the Raptor (Crown of Predation)</b><br /> The character may ignore surrender and does not suffer the Beaten Down tilt; conversely, the Beaten Down and Surrender rules are still in force for her opponents even if she are trying to kill them. Additionally, she adds her Life dots as dice to any rolls for Down and Dirty combat.<br /> _<br /> <br /> <b>Crown of [Fate]</b><br /> description<br /> <br /> <b>Crown of Agency</b><br /> The character may ignore the effects of Status Merits or Destiny dice used directly against her, up to her Time dots. The Seer may also ignore one point of Withstand when using the Temporal Sympathy Attainment.<br /> _<br /> <br /> <b>Crown of [Death]</b><br /> description<br /> <br /> <b>Crown of Scarcity</b><br /> The character disregards the equipment bonus of items and uses their Resources cost instead. She may also have a number of dedicated magical tools equal to her dots in Matter. (I changed this slightly to be symmetrical with the others)<br /> _<br /> <br /> So, we lack the Psychopomp and the Ruin's Crowns.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T06:46:09-07:00","id":904922,"title":"","content":"What was Psychopomp's shtick?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T06:52:59-07:00","id":904926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=904922#post904922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What was Psychopomp's shtick?</div> </div> </div> </div>In order to enter the afterlife, one must be X and not Y.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T06:56:11-07:00","id":904927,"title":"","content":"From the old forums, Words from the Brookshaw on the Prophet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>David Brookshaw</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Prophet, remember, is all about the bogus but pervasive idea of the &quot;Great Man&quot; view of history - He tells Her followers that only select individuals have any agency to change the world, while the mass of people are doomed to follow along behind the pedagogue of the current flavour. Her followers both try to become &quot;Great Men&quot; and identify and neutralise the same among their enemies - they're the sorts to kill the leader of a rebellion, identify the guru who's attracting Pentacle mages to their banner and do away with or subvert them. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Crown Prelacy for the Prophet would be about assuming that mantle of leadership and destiny, the Sword Prelacy is about identifying and countering it in others and the Temple Prelacy creates areas of &quot;gravity&quot; that such individuals are drawn to; a Seer of the Prophet would find people flocking to their banner while they set up base in a Temple to that Exarch, while other Seers use Time Prelacy Temple Stones to set traps for Great Men they disapprove of.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T06:57:17-07:00","id":904929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=904922#post904922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What was Psychopomp's shtick?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Death\u2019s Seal commands souls. <br /> Barring them from Stygia\u2019s release, it condemns them <br /> to abide in numerous incarnations or erode into gray <br /> shades. If there is a heaven, the Psychopomp guards <br /> the way with a sword, and will only let the greatest <br /> Seers enter.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T07:07:56-07:00","id":904935,"title":"","content":"My first gut instinct would be something that interacts with victim's Resolve when they might stray from the &quot;right&quot; path, but that doesn't sound that useful for Death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T17:06:18-07:00","id":905268,"title":"","content":"Maybe...<br /> When opposing the Prelate, his opponents - both in social, physical, magical and mental challenges - suffer Beaten Down Tilt unless lower of their Resolve/Composure is higher than Prelate's Death Arcanum. This Tilt represents overpowering fear of being excluded from the afterlife...or worse. The Tilt is appropriately modified to fit situations outside of combat - instead of violent actions, victim may not take actions that would go against Exarch's agenda without spending the willpower point. If Prelate spends a point of Mana, Tilt may work even on character that are normally immune to it - because of their supernatural origins, because their life is at stake, and so on. This does *not* allow to skip the Composure/Resolve requirement. <br /> Crown of Dread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 06-01-2016, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T12:50:48-07:00","id":911057,"title":"","content":"Here's some ideas for Crown Attainments on my end. One is a version of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a>'s Crown of Boundaries. While two (the Crowns of Denial and Corruption) are a 2E Conversion of 1E Homebrew from King of the Hill. <hr /><br /> The Nemesis grants the <b>Crown of Boundaries</b>. When conducting social maneuvering with spirits, the Seer raises his first impression with them by half his Spirit dots, rounded up. Furthermore, he may choose to raise or lower the Gauntlet Strength of his surroundings by half his Spirit dots, rounded up.<br /> <br /> The Psychopomp grants the <b>Crown of Denial</b>. The Seer is considered to be an anchor for any and all ghosts within sensory range, and can choose to inflict a penalty to their Manifestations and Numina equal to her Death dots. When interacting with a ghost, she automatically what conditions must be fulfilled for him to resolve his anchors.<br /> <br /> The Prophet grants the <b>Crown of Judgement</b>. The Seer adds his Time dots to the Withstand ratings of his Temporal Sympathy. Conversely, he halves the Withstand ratings of those targeted by his spells through Temporal Sympathy.<br /> <br /> The Ruin grants the <b>Crown of Corruption</b>. When carrying out actions which carry out the Exarch's Mystery Commands, the Seer's enemies suffer a penalty equal to his Fate dots on all attempts to oppose him. Furthermore, when using the Conditional Duration Attainment, double the levels of Duration given by a condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 06-09-2016, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T14:43:08-07:00","id":911157,"title":"","content":"Psychopomp might grant the ability to mark a target s.t. if it dies under the effect it will automatically come back as a ghost anchored to him or a temple. (That might be a better temple effect) Commanding ghosts could be a fitting crown.<br /> <br /> Prophet could have a Crown that allows them to subvert any action performed by those lacking Destiny. (Prophet could <i>grant</i> Destiny, too.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T02:31:15-07:00","id":916742,"title":"","content":"I'd really like to see what a Prelacy of The Gate would look like, since it's probably coming up in my game soon.<br /> <br /> So far it looks like the ideas are; something to manipulate Paradox rolls, and something that would benefit both Openers and Closers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T03:24:45-07:00","id":916754,"title":"","content":"I'd say that you'd subtract your dots in &lt;BLANK&gt; from your Gnosis for the purposes of how many dice Reach adds to your Paradox pool, and you can summon Abyssal entities without everything automatically going tits up (use the system for Supernal summoning, I guess?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T03:42:53-07:00","id":916757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=916754#post916754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say that you'd subtract your dots in &lt;BLANK&gt; from your Gnosis for the purposes of how many dice Reach adds to your Paradox pool, and you can summon Abyssal entities without everything automatically going tits up (use the system for Supernal summoning, I guess?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this. I also had another idea while I was prepping for the next session.<br /> <br /> What about something that lets you use the existing system for controlling (not containing) paradox when <i>other</i> mages cause one? It'd use the same system as letting the abyss into your own spells would, except you'd roll your Gnosis when another nearby mage releases a paradox. You'd then decide how the Paradox Reach is spent per usual, which would allow you to summon an abyssal entity or environment(by spending Reach for that effect) or stop one from being summoned (by spending the Reach on other things)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T08:21:44-07:00","id":916847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=916757#post916757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this. I also had another idea while I was prepping for the next session.<br /> <br /> What about something that lets you use the existing system for controlling (not containing) paradox when <i>other</i> mages cause one? It'd use the same system as letting the abyss into your own spells would, except you'd roll your Gnosis when another nearby mage releases a paradox. You'd then decide how the Paradox Reach is spent per usual, which would allow you to summon an abyssal entity or environment(by spending Reach for that effect) or stop one from being summoned (by spending the Reach on other things)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My idea was adding something to your gnosis (perhaps half gnosis rounded up) for the purposes of paradox control and being able to spend mana to increase paradox die on your own and other mage's paradox rolls on a one for one basis (just like how the core mage can decrease their own paradox dice pools with mana).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T17:05:09-08:00","id":1157399,"title":"","content":"As a thought, The Prophet's Crown should probably allow for a select amount of automatic successes equal to Time per [duration], cementing their place as fixtures of history and actual agents of agency. Alternatively, they might be able to take the shine from other's successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T21:14:43-08:00","id":1159336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1157215-crown-prelacy-attainments-collaboration#post1157215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crowns I have cobbled together<br /> <br /> Chancellor - Exarch of Matter<br /> The Chancellor (Mammon) grants the Crown of Wealth. The character adds her Matter dots to their Resources for purposes of applying soft leverage, making purchases and availability. When someone accepts soft leverage from the character, the character regains a Mana.<br /> Nemesis - Exarch of Spirit<br /> The Nemesis grants the Crown of Veils. The character benefits that spirits must subtract the character's Spirit dots from any roll concerning the character, from perceiving him, recalling anything about him, or attempting to affect him in anyway. The character also has no naturally occurring Resonant conditions and may reflexively invoke a Clash of Wills on attempts to establish such a Condition.<br /> Prophet - Exarch of Time<br /> The Prophet grants the Crown of Greatness. The character adds his Time dots to their Destiny, which may exceed the standard limits of that merit. When regaining Willpower from the Destiny's Doom also regain a Mana.<br /> Psychopomp - Exarch of Death<br /> The Psychopomp grants the Crown of Woe. When someone is attempting to open the character's Doors using one or more Merits, the Seer may reduce each of her opponent\u2019s social Merits by her Death dots, denying the use of any techniques \u201clost\u201d by instinctively ignoring them with a death hardened heart.<br /> Raptor - Exarch of Life<br /> The Raptor grants the Crown of Carnality. The character gains an additional Vice, and regains one point of Mana every time she gains Willpower through either Vice. Also, she may apply Soft Leverage through preternaturally potent sexual favors in Social maneuvering, counting her Life dots and Striking Looks Merits as if they were Resources for that purpose.<br /> Ruin - Exarch of Fate<br /> The Ruin grants the Crown of Banality. The character benefits that everyone must subtract the character's Fate dots from any roll to learn anything about him that isn't solely mundane and banal. Supernatural attempts to make the character stand out or seem special may be reflexively resisted by a Clash of Wills. In particular the seer's active supernatural effects don't alert Peripheral Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> <br /> I am very interested feed back and what other people have come up with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't see this thread and made my own, someone was kind enough to link me to this thread so I am reposting here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T05:04:35-07:00","id":1320249,"title":"","content":"Page 122 of Signs of Sorcery has three new official Crowns Scaricty (Chancellor ), Instinct (Raptor) and Agency (Prophet)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T05:36:32-07:00","id":1320252,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't mind someone cobbling together a new version of the Crown of Instinct since surrendering/beaten down is an optional rules system. Beaten Down also has other sources, but the optional system should be by far the most common source so kinda underwhelming for anyone who doesn't use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T07:45:11-07:00","id":1320275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=1320252#post1320252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't mind someone cobbling together a new version of the Crown of Instinct since surrendering/beaten down is an optional rules system. Beaten Down also has other sources, but the optional system should be by far the most common source so kinda underwhelming for anyone who doesn't use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The lack of wound penalties and extra Doors are a nice touch though.<br /> <br /> I'm a tad confused with the utility of the Agency Crown. Temporal Sympathy to one's personal history doesn't seem like it would come up often and the scaling benefit appears to counter when said Sympathy is used against the Prelate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T15:59:40-07:00","id":1320599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=1320275#post1320275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lack of wound penalties and extra Doors are a nice touch though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's something but it's not nearly enough, imo. Ignoring wound penalties and adding extra Doors are both represented through mundane Merits. All the other Crowns adds a supernatural advantage that is difficult to get through other means (short of casting a spell to replicate the effect).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T22:28:36-07:00","id":1320664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=1320275#post1320275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a tad confused with the utility of the Agency Crown. Temporal Sympathy to one's personal history doesn't seem like it would come up often and the scaling benefit appears to counter when said Sympathy is used against the Prelate.</div> </div> </div> </div>It probably makes more sense in light of SoS saying that most Mages have their Temporal Sympathy to life before Awakening reduced to Weak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T02:12:41-07:00","id":1320693,"title":"","content":"Well, everyone's temporal sympathy ranges from connected to weak, iirc. The weird part is that it works for everyone without distinction, creating an advantage that can just as much become a weakness. But I think the Eye Crown worked similarly (unless asymmetrical sympathy is a thing) so maybe not that weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T07:32:52-07:00","id":1320742,"title":"","content":"That's probably the reason there's a time delay before time magic kicks in. If the Prelate doesn't want to be affected by someone then they have a chance to do something about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T08:00:44-07:00","id":1320752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=1320742#post1320742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's probably the reason there's a time delay before time magic kicks in. If the Prelate doesn't want to be affected by someone then they have a chance to do something about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately that's also a two edged sword (as currently written; not saying that it's intended). It's far less likely to be an issue since people shouldn't know that much about the effects of your Crown and thus be unlikely to plan around it, but it's potentially possible for an enemy to retroactively set the building you're in on fire. The rest of your Pylon shifts outside because they'd never enter a building that is on fire, but you're stuck alone in the middle of a burning building for your Time dots turns. Similarly your own spells aren't exempt from the Crown, meaning that you might find yourself in a disadvantageous situation, say an ambush, that you wish to retroactively fix by never walking into that ambush in the first place, but you're stuck taking fire for your Time dots turns before the spell takes effect for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T12:09:53-07:00","id":1320808,"title":"","content":"I feel pretty sure the time delay can or should be able to be waived.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T17:53:26-07:00","id":1383481,"title":"","content":"Ritual Thread Necromancy!<br /> <br /> The Dark Eras 2 preview has our 8th officially published Crown attainment; <b>Secrets </b>(Nemesis)!<br /> Which is very different from what the ideas in this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T04:03:48-07:00","id":1383549,"title":"","content":"So with most of the Iron Seals being covered (with the exception of the Gate, the Ruin and the Psychopomp), what about Crowns for the lesser Exarchs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T18:13:00-07:00","id":1383700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=1383549#post1383549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So with most of the Iron Seals being covered (with the exception of the Gate, the Ruin and the Psychopomp), what about Crowns for the lesser Exarchs?</div> </div> </div> </div>What are the lesser Exarchs? Do we have anything to go off of?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T18:33:41-07:00","id":1383703,"title":"","content":"Well, I know in Signs of Sorcery they say (according to Seer doctrine, which we should absolutly take with a grain of salt) there's an Iron Seal representing each of the 10 arcana and the Abyss for the Greater Exarchs, 4 of which are the Archgenitors who are patron to the Great Ministires (who have &quot;always existed.&quot;) Under them are countless lesser Exarchs and lesser divine servitors and saints who obey the commands of the greater Exarchs. <br /> <br /> What that means for Crown attainment wise...well this is more speculation than anything but just like the Greater Exarchs compete for having their symbolism dominant in the Fallen world and thus rise above the rest as Archgenitors, perhaps the lesser Exarchs compete amongst each other to replace the tyrannical symbolism that defines the greater Iron Seal for each of the Arcanum? After all, the &quot;As above, so below&quot; pyramid structure is greatly used by the Seers already. There may have been many times throughout history that an Iron Seal's symbolism was &quot;rediscovered&quot; to be a more prevalent form of tyranny for that particular Arcanum.<br /> <br /> In short: Just change the Crown Attainment to reflect another use for the already pre-existing one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":". 04-24-2020, 09:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T04:57:15-07:00","id":1383750,"title":"","content":"It's straight up canon that there exists Exarchs other than the 10+1. The Dethroned Queen is one who was allegedly killed. Any Ascended Seers would also become Exarchs by definition since they'd become Supernal entities of Tyranny. Then there's just regular Supernal entities of Tyranny who never were mages, either in the Time Before or in the Fallen World, who'd also be Exarchs. More info can be found in the Seers of the Throne book.<br /> Anyway, we don't really know why the Exarchs are the only ones (that we know of) that grant Prelacies, and I don't think we know if that's something all Exarchs can do. Signs of Sorcery might provide some clues since it describes how someone might get a Prelacy, but I'm not at my copy right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T05:43:33-07:00","id":1383755,"title":"","content":"...okay...so it is time to figure out the Crown of the Dethrowned Queen then.<br /> Guess I'll reread Reign of the Exarchs again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T09:28:06-07:00","id":1383782,"title":"","content":"According to SoS, some among the Lesser Exarchs are the Monarch, the Rani, the Stranger, the Traveler, the Mother, the Cannibal, the Destroyer, the Tutor, the Judge, the Progenitor, the Surgeon, the Hierophant and the Predator. It is unknown which of those is an actual separate Exarch and which is a minor manifestation of (or even just another name to) a major Iron Seal, but the Rani and the Progenitor are ascended Seers, at the very least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-29T06:19:11-07:00","id":1420807,"title":"","content":"The Psychopomp grants the <b>Crown of Denial</b>. The character can Scour his Pattern one additional time per day. The character also can destroy a ghost\u2019s Anchor as a Blood Sacrifice to regain the ghost\u2019s Integrity plus his dots in Death Arcanum in Mana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Swing on the spiral of our divinity and still be a human&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25961-redzone","name":"Redzone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T08:42:36-08:00","id":1422036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=1383782#post1383782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to SoS, some among the Lesser Exarchs are the Monarch, the Rani, the Stranger, the Traveler, the Mother, the Cannibal, the Destroyer, the Tutor, the Judge, the Progenitor, the Surgeon, the Hierophant and the Predator. It is unknown which of those is an actual separate Exarch and which is a minor manifestation of (or even just another name to) a major Iron Seal, but the Rani and the Progenitor are ascended Seers, at the very least.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm curious: &quot;Rani&quot; as an (sort of) Hindu queen?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Swing on the spiral of our divinity and still be a human&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25961-redzone","name":"Redzone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T09:10:17-08:00","id":1422046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redzone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=1422036#post1422036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm curious: &quot;Rani&quot; as an (sort of) Hindu queen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. It appears to be a reference to DaveB's first AP, Broken Diamond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T15:59:17-08:00","id":1422140,"title":"","content":"Also a Doctor Who villain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T19:58:08-08:00","id":1422366,"title":"","content":"The Ruin grants the <b>Crown of Entropy</b>. The Curse of Quiescence is stronger in the character's surroundings: Sleepers rolls Integrity plus the character's dot rating in Fate arcanum to see the effects of Dissonance. Also, whenever a Sleeper loses Integrity due a breaking point related to obvious magic in the character's surroundings, the character regains 1 Mana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Swing on the spiral of our divinity and still be a human&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25961-redzone","name":"Redzone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-27T19:48:54-08:00","id":1426417,"title":"","content":"The Ruin grants the <b>Crown of Epicaricacy</b>, which makes Conditional Duration cost no mana to use. Furthermore, the Prelate designs a Doom when they receive it. Anyone who dispels or ends one of their spells is afflicted by it for the remainder of the spell's duration. This can be changed every time they fulfill their Mystery Command.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-28T08:14:41-08:00","id":1426465,"title":"","content":"The Psychopomp grants the <b>Crown of Judgement</b>. When encountering a ghost of Rank 2 without Anchors, the Prelate can spend a mana to create and force a Deathmask upon them, alongside one of their Obsessions. This grants up to [Death] Ranks when worn, with no ghost going beyond Rank 5. Once they fulfill it, the Reaper loses the Obsession, keeps the Deathmask and is free to carry on as they see fit. A Prelate can only have one such being bound at a time.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the Prelate gains the Descend Numen. Unlike the normal version, up to [Death] ghosts without the Numen can be employed. Alternatively, it can also be used by performing a Demesne creating ritual, which contains up to [Death] soul stones. The Prelate must pay 3 mana to use this effect, plus an additional 3 for each of these &quot;inert&quot; participants.<br /> <br /> For example, using it with 3 ghosts without the Numen, one with, plus the mage would cost 12 mana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 11-28-2020, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-28T13:44:56-08:00","id":1426492,"title":"","content":"You got the name right! But not the effects of it. You're getting warmer, though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (The Ruin's Crown is &quot;Excellence&quot;, by the way)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-28T14:50:27-08:00","id":1426501,"title":"","content":"Cool, glad to see I am getting closer. The <b>Crown of Excellence </b>sounds like one which would upgrade a chance dice to a normal one. It would also allow one to upgrade a mundane successes into exceptional ones, with Willpower expenditure allowing them to affect spellcasting rolls.<br /> <br /> Another idea for the <b>Crown of Judgement</b> is that it could allow the Prelate to spend a mana to become the sole Anchor to a ghost of up to [Death] Rank (with ones above Rank 5 being immune should they ever attain archmastery) and define how it can be resolved. Should they decide to end the effect, the ghost is considered to have no Anchors and is dragged down to the Great Below (at least until they figure out a way to reach any of their surviving Anchors). In addition, for [Death] times a day, destroying an Anchor counts as a ritual sacrifice and grants the ghost's current Integrity as mana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 11-28-2020, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T12:32:49-08:00","id":1433822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=1426492#post1426492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You got the name right! But not the effects of it. You're getting warmer, though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (The Ruin's Crown is &quot;Excellence&quot;, by the way)</div> </div> </div> </div>I am necrothreading but I didn't see if you responded. I am about to plan a Mage the Awakening game and I wondered what kind of crown/prelacy The Gate would give.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T13:25:14-08:00","id":1433829,"title":"","content":"The Gate grants the <b>Crown of Delimitation</b>, which allows Prelates to cast befouled spells without risking Wisdom and grants [Spirit] bonus dice to the Paradox control roll.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, they can spend a mana to gain immunity to Paradox Environmental Conditions for a scene.<br /> <br /> The name is a reference to Horos/Stauros, with their function as setting limits. But since the Secret Order of the Gate already has the Realm of Liminarity, I thought this name could synergize with their role within it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T14:54:02-08:00","id":1433841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=1433822#post1433822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am necrothreading but I didn't see if you responded. I am about to plan a Mage the Awakening game and I wondered what kind of crown/prelacy The Gate would give.</div> </div> </div> </div>I stand with the 1st edition approach of the Gate having Legacies rather than Prelacies, but I am in the minority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T14:58:19-08:00","id":1433842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=1433841#post1433841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I stand with the 1st edition approach of the Gate having Legacies rather than Prelacies, but I am in the minority.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not both?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T15:14:58-08:00","id":1433843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=1433842#post1433842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not both?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, it is because I subscribe to the hinted at idea that the Gate isn't an Exarch the way the others are, perhaps even being some sort of Abyssal being. The fact that it was included at all among their number feels more like a concession from the other Exarchs, rather than an acknowledgement of a peer.<br /> <br /> But you are right, there is no reason why a different, argubly more valid version of the Gate can't have a Pralacy and Legacies devoted to it.<br /> Though that does imply the other Exarchs should have Legacies too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T15:19:33-08:00","id":1433844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=1433843#post1433843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, it is because I subscribe to the hinted at idea that the Gate isn't an Exarch the way the others are, perhaps even being some sort of Abyssal being. The fact that it was included at all among their number feels more like a concession from the other Exarchs, rather than an acknowledgement of a peer.<br /> <br /> But you are right, there is no reason why a different, argubly more valid version of the Gate can't have a Pralacy and Legacies devoted to it.<br /> Though that does imply the other Exarchs should have Legacies too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I also view the Gate as somewhat.. different from the Exarchs. We could always say that Her Prelacy represents Her &quot;Exarch visage&quot;, as being accepted to the Exarchs yet not actually being a part of them, while her Legacies represent Her more &quot;true&quot; nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T15:22:30-08:00","id":1433845,"title":"","content":"One does certainly not preclude the other. The Secret Order of the Gate Legacy is a cult devoted to the Gate. A Prelate of the Gate, however, is someone the Gate has taken interest in, quite possibly without the Seer necessarily wanting such attention in the first place. The two concepts can certainly overlap, but they can also serve different roles within the same game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T17:17:11-08:00","id":1433857,"title":"","content":"That could be interesting. The Prelate is chosen by the Gate marking their soul as an unusual result of a Paradox condition. The Secret Order of the Gate could be commanded to recruit them, independent of past alliances. But its with them that lies the secret to excisibg the Prelacy, should the chosen abhor it. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, they could be told to guide them, with the Prelate not necessarily knowing this, but never letting them join the inner circle. <br /> <br /> It could lead to all sorts of unique dynamics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T06:56:36-07:00","id":1513950,"title":"","content":"Further thread Necromancy!<br /> Tome of the Pentacle has a new prelacy.<br /> The Ruin (Kyrian and Peirasmon) grants the Crown of Inevitability on pg 142.<br /> <br /> In the discussion thread, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> said <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1511880-tome-of-the-pentacle-on-dtrpg?p=1513362#post1513362\">stuff related to the Psychpomp's Crown.</a> Though I have no idea what the Giest rules referenced are. The simple question thread suggests that Integrity 10 people don't leave Ghosts, but this isn't stated in my copy of the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T07:05:31-07:00","id":1514695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments?p=1513950#post1513950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Further thread Necromancy!<br /> Tome of the Pentacle has a new prelacy.<br /> The Ruin (Kyrian and Peirasmon) grants the Crown of Inevitability on pg 142.<br /> <br /> In the discussion thread, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> said <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1511880-tome-of-the-pentacle-on-dtrpg?p=1513362#post1513362\">stuff related to the Psychpomp's Crown.</a> Though I have no idea what the Giest rules referenced are. The simple question thread suggests that Integrity 10 people don't leave Ghosts, but this isn't stated in my copy of the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Integrity 10 ppl not leaving ghosts is indeed my understanding.<br /> <br /> I think the book states what rank of a ghost is left behind, for people their integrity determines the rank, for animals or buildings it depends on whether a breaking point was caused (with the rank depending on whether integrity was lost or not. As far as i recall.<br /> <br /> I think that is in Geist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}